"prose": [
{
"from": 111,
"to": 123,
"text": "The window boot smoke runs: Tauri 2.11.0 → 2.12.5 and tao 0.35.0 → 0.37.2 move the window runtime (the boot self-end closed at 2026-10-10 was measured against tao 0.35's device-event thread, obs-plan history). The console engine's runtime gate is one engine cycle, since DuckDB, tokio and rustls move under it (obs-plan §10: a lockfile-only DuckDB bump has changed runtime behaviour before). The webview gates run because `pulse-app/ui/package-lock.json` changes. No procedure is added or changed, so the bindings close is the procedure-preserving form: `capability-drift` before the workspace run, the regen as the last cargo-adjacent step, then `git diff --quiet` against the chunk base (test-plan §3). No headful self-verify is listed: `cargo xtask self-verify` drives WebView2 through `msedgedriver` on a Windows host, and this Linux host has none; the boot series and the CI a11y job stand in for the UI half. `cargo xtask test:a11y` is not a local entry (the Playwright headless shell is not installed on this host, measured at the previous chunk's P5); the CI `a11y` job runs it with its regression detector and is read by name in the CI read, and locally the suite's config-named `--list` entry guards against a list-time import failure. `cargo auditable build --workspace --release` is the CI `supply-chain` job's last step and is read there. Lean checks per `inputs#I1`: the gates this plan requires, each run once."
},
